From: teeworlds-rl <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:35:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] RL bridge protocol v2: spatial observation and seeded spawns

Phase 2 of the teeworlds-rl project. Actions are unchanged; the
observation becomes fixed size, normalized and local.

- Per agent: a 33x25 tile window of collision bytes (solid, death,
  no hook) centered on the agent, cut from a copy of the map made once,
  and a 67 float vector: own movement and combat state, the opponent
  only inside the rectangle a human client would be sent (with a line
  of fire bit from CCollision::IntersectLine), the four nearest
  projectiles in view and the episode progress. A raw state block is
  kept for tests and logging.
- HELLO sends the map's collision once so the trainer can check grids.
- The first spawn of an episode puts the agents on two different map
  spawn points from the bridge's own seeded generator, through one hook
  in CPlayer::TryRespawn that only applies while the bridge runs.
  Respawns and everything without the bridge are unchanged.
